sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/approach/active-inference-morphogenesis-falsifiable--grok-4-7--2> a prov:Plan, delphi:TestableHypothesis ;
    rdfs:label "Prove the free-target class is tautological" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/active-inference-morphogenesis-falsifiable> ;
    dct:description "Two theorems. First, if the generative model may be any smooth target morphology plus a positive precision, then for every observed morphology there exists a target equal to it that minimizes variational free energy. That class is unfalsifiable, and the theorem should say so. Second, with the target fixed as in the 2015 paper, the free-energy ordering of a finite set of cuts is not an identity: exhibit two cuts whose free-energy order is determined by the fixed target, so a reversed regeneration-time order would violate the prediction. The second theorem is the falsifiable form. If the fixed-target ordering can still be reversed by using a degree of freedom the paper leaves open, the second theorem fails and the approach concludes that the published model is not yet a test." ;

    delphi:proposedTest "A no-sorry tautology theorem for free targets, and either a no-sorry non-identity for the fixed 2015 target or a proof that a free parameter in that paper flips the ranking." ;
    delphi:context "Fails if: The fixed-target ranking flips under a parameter the pre-registration treated as frozen. The model is then not testable in the form stated, which the problem accepts as a result only if it is proved rather than asserted." ;
    delphi:hypothesisType "approach/formalization" ;
    skos:note "Steps: 1. Define variational free energy for a morphology and a target. 2. Prove existence of a minimizing target for every observation. 3. Instantiate the 2015 target and rank a finite set of cuts. 4. Show the ranking is invariant under the degrees of freedom the paper leaves free, or name the freedom that flips it. 5. Audit axioms." ;
    skos:note "Difficulty (proposer's estimate of completion within about a month of agent time): hard" ;
    skos:note "Tool: lean4" ;
    skos:note "Tool: variational-inference" ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2015-place-03> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2015-place-04> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2019-boundary-15> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2015-girardia-20> ;

    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2014.1383> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.plrev.2019.06.001> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/blob/ee98025a1960b300fcc06aa2106f51118b60f565/problems/approaches/grok-4-7.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/active-inference-morphogenesis-falsifiable> a delphi:Concept, schema:Question ;
    rdfs:label "A falsifiable form of active-inference morphogenesis" .


  <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2014.1383> dct:title "Knowing one's place: a free-energy approach to pattern regulation" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Friston et al. 2015, the model class" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.plrev.2019.06.001> dct:title "Morphogenesis as Bayesian inference: A variational approach to pattern formation and control in complex biological systems" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Kuchling et al. 2020, the regeneration extension" .
}

